    rdfs:label "urn:silmaril:entity#instances.papers.21_ologs_and_typed_english.chapters.01_olog_as_typed_english.sections.03_mittens_olog_walkthrough.concrete_anchor_3_BodyMassQualityBox#bodymassqualitybox" .
silm:instances_papers_21_ologs_and_typed_english_chapters_01_olog_as_typed_english_sections_03_mittens_olog_walkthrough_concrete_anchor_3_BodyMassQualityBox#bodymassqualitybox silm:hasLongDescription "The BodyMassQualityBox is the typed-noun box for the body mass quality (e.g., 4.5 kg as a quality, not a number). In the paper's apparatus it appears as the symbol 'BodyMassQualityBox', a concrete instance grounded in the Mittens domain story; it serves as the anchor whose semantics every diagram, formula, and prose reference back to." .
